+# CP-to-SDK verified HTTP test
+
+This test compiles the actual CP HTTP helper, checked BMP commit and SDK
+SecureClient/SecureHttpClient against a synthetic TLS server on 127.0.0.1.
+The server observes a synthetic Authorization marker; no account or service
+credentials are used. Temporary certificates and keys are removed on exit.
+
+The paired SDK patch adds a proposed backend capability. The runner also compiles
+an unmodified copy of the pinned SDK HEAD and the patched SDK without wolfSSL.
+Both must reject the opt-in without opening a connection. Legacy HTTP behavior
+remains unchanged, including its existing lack of peer verification.
+
+Requirements: C++20 compiler, Python 3 with `cryptography`, OpenSSL-backed Python
+`ssl`, ArduinoJson 7.4.2 headers and the pinned Arduino-wolfSSL host library.
+Build that library with the reproducible helper in the source-review package;
+the SDK source and headers must match the library settings.
+
+```
+python3 test/plugin_verified_tls/run.py \
+  --wolf-root /path/to/Arduino-wolfSSL \
+  --wolf-archive /path/to/libwolfssl-host.a \
+  --arduinojson /path/to/ArduinoJson/src \
+  --output /path/to/result.json
+```
+
+Cases cover request, download, password token mint, wrong hostname, untrusted CA,
+malformed CA, expired certificate, stale clock, invalid BMP, old SDK, disabled
+backend and legacy compatibility. The actual event drain and shared retry budget
+are tested separately by `plugin_verified_http`; this runner supplies a controlled
+clock proof and in-memory storage. It does not establish real SNTP timing, device
+heap, energy, SD durability or displayed pixels. Loopback transport uses POSIX
+sockets; the wolfSSL host library omits ESP-specific acceleration and allocators.
